      "side": 1,
      "message": "Potentially a very stupid question, but why do you need to create a compat version here and explicitly set it in the CTDownloader, instead of relying on the mCTDownloader.start() API (and then doing mCTDownloader.stop() in tearDown())?\n\nOtherwise, it feels like the unit tests are testing class internals rather than testing via the available APIs. This makes the unit tests less resilient to implementation changes, because the unit tests are relying on implementation details like this method.\n\nInstead, it\u0027s recommended to exercise the behavior via the public APIs, and avoid the use of `@VisibleForTesting` on methods and unnecessarily increasing the visibility of methods.\n\ngo/java-practices/visibility#test_apis\ngo/unit-test-practices#public-apis\nhttp://sites/codehealth/refactoring-gallery/visiblefortesting-smellyviolationofencapsulation\n\nThen, the existing tests could remain with calling startMetadataDownload() and startContentDownload() without needing a CompatVersion passed in.",
